commit a0c1f61036c30b217e86285484ec493dc2d688ac
Author: Stefan Lindblad <stefan.lindblad@linux.com>
Date:   Mon Oct 5 14:12:43 2026 +0000

    fix(engine): use RUSTUP_TOOLCHAIN to locate the provisioned Rust toolchain
    
    rustup is installed as a manager whose toolchain tree was never
    registered as a default, so 'rustup which cargo' failed and every
    host-side resolution (resolve_cargo_toolchain, rustup_run) falsely
    reported 'no Rust toolchain'.
    
    Set RUSTUP_TOOLCHAIN=/rust/toolchain on every rustup invocation so it
    uses the real provisioned tree as the active toolchain, and
    RUSTUP_OFFLINE=true so any toolchain download attempt fails closed
    instead of reaching for the network. No symlink, no write to the
    read-only /rust/toolchain mount, no dependence on volatile /tmp
    state. This is a language-agnostic pattern: it works for any host
    toolchain that ships its own 'use the bound toolchain' switch.
    
    Fixes toolchain::tests::ensure_toolchain_records_the_default_toolchain.

